# Verified release channel (spec §11). The committed gate artifacts under
# dist/gate/ are the off-machine trust anchor: the approver cross-checks the
# Telegram banner hash against dist/gate/sshgate-gate-linux-amd64.sha256 on
# github.com (§11.5). `binary` (= -text -diff -merge) guarantees git never
# applies CRLF/EOL normalization or textual diff/merge to these paths, so the
# committed bytes hash to EXACTLY what `make release-gate` produced and CI
# re-verifies — a normalization would silently change the published hash.
dist/gate/* binary
